ull,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null},{"crn":"73097","code":"MPM","typeCode":"LBD","group":"lab","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Laboratory-Discussion","typeCode":"LBD","days":["M","W"],"start":780,"end":1010,"location":"327 Temple Hoyne Buell Hall","instructors":["McGuire, M"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null},{"crn":"73099","code":"ZT","typeCode":"LBD","group":"lab","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Laboratory-Discussion","typeCode":"LBD","days":["M","W"],"start":780,"end":1010,"location":"319 Temple Hoyne Buell Hall","instructors":["Tao, Z"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"LA 545","subject":"LA","number":"545","title":"Graduate Internship","creditHours":"0 TO 12 hours","minHours":0,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Approved for S/U grading only. May be repeated in separate semesters to a maximum of 12 hours. Prerequisite: Restricted to graduate students in Landscape Architecture.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"75451","code":"A","typeCode":"INT","group":"int","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Internship","typeCode":"INT","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":["Davis, L"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"LA 587","subject":"LA","number":"587","title":"Graduate Seminar","creditHours":"1 TO 4 hours","minHours":1,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Additional fees may apply. See Class Schedule. May be repeated if topics vary. Prerequisite: Consent of instructor.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"35332","code":"BD","typeCode":"ONL","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Online","typeCode":"ONL","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"n.a.","instructors":["Deal, B"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"This course will provide an overview of energy as it relates to landscape and landscape design from global to community perspectives. Students will generally understand energy systems and urban landscapes, its impact on climate, and potential community scaled responses and how to apply it in design. This is an asynchronous online course."},{"crn":"46648","code":"DH","typeCode":"SEM","group":"sem","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Seminar","typeCode":"SEM","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"325 Temple Hoyne Buell Hall","instructors":["Hays, D"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":"Instructor Approval Required","sectionText":"As a relationship between humans and nature, landscape is not bound to any specific medium. Instead, it is negotiated through a wide range of media. This seminar examines the theory and practice of landscape as a relational condition. Participants will explore twelve works of landscape in diverse media in order to understand how their terms are defined and negotiated. Through shared firsthand experience, close analysis, and interpretation, with pertinent scholarly supports, students will address questions of agency, purpose, and meaning alongside practical concerns such as materiality, technique, and context. As a semester-long project, each student will develop and self-publish an original zine in a print edition of 20, interpreting and influencing the contemporary situation of landscape through a lens of personal understandings, priorities, and aspirations."},{"crn":"40699","code":"RG","typeCode":"LEC","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture","typeCode":"LEC","days":["T","R"],"start":570,"end":620,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":["Ginsburg, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"History of prison architecture, landscapes, and carceral regimes from ancient times until the present. Topics include: philosophy of punishment, the invention of the modern prison, the advent of mass incarceration, and 21st century geographies of incarceration. The course focuses on the western experience, but also includes international examples, e.g. from China, East Africa, and Japan. Interdisciplinary approach includes readings in architectural history, urban planning, sociology, philosophy, psychology, history, and landscape studies."}]},{"id":"LA 590","subject":"LA","number":"590","title":"Directed Research","creditHours":"1 TO 8 hours","minHours":1,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Additional fees may apply. See Class Schedule. Approved for Letter and S/U grading. May be repeated. Prerequisite: Consent of instructor.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"10489","code":"","typeCode":"IND","group":"ind","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Independent Study","typeCode":"IND","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":"Instructor Approval Required","sectionText":null},{"crn":"40701","code":"RG1","typeCode":"LEC","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture","typeCode":"LEC","days":["T","R"],"start":540,"end":620,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":["Ginsburg, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"LA 594","subject":"LA","number":"594","title":"Cultural Heritage","creditHours":"2 OR 4 hours","minHours":2,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as ANTH 594. May be repeated in separate terms to a maximum of 16 hours but no more than 10 hours in any one term. Prerequisite: Concurrent enrollment in LA 438 may be required in the spring semester; check Class Schedule.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"43298","code":"KH","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T"],"start":840,"end":1010,"location":"325 Temple Hoyne Buell Hall","instructors":["Holliday, K"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to students with Graduate class standing."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"Travel to Granada, Spain over spring break is required for the course. Student transportation, lodging, some meals and some admission fees to museums will be covered by the Department of Landscape Architecture."}]},{"id":"LA 597","subject":"LA","number":"597","title":"Research Design & Methods","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"64182","code":"PR","typeCode":"LEC","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture","typeCode":"LEC","days":["M","W"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"325 Temple Hoyne Buell Hall","instructors":["Rhee, P"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"LA 598","subject":"LA","number":"598","title":"Master's Project","creditHours":"0 TO 8 hours","minHours":0,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Approved for letter and S/U grading. Prerequisite: Consent of instructor and program adviser.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"10490","code":"","typeCode":"IND","group":"ind","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Independent Study","typeCode":"IND","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instruct